{
  "note": "Conduit additions to the served Apollo-shaped GraphQL interface. No Hub answered for any of these GRAPHQL COORDINATES, and that is the only thing every entry here has in common. Beyond it they differ, and the citation says how. publishedAs means Apollo itself names this field: in the pinned OpenAPI, in an apollo-cli flag, or on a SIBLING TYPE IN THE RECOVERY RECORD -- `apollo-graphql ApolloEnvironmentPage.nextPageToken` is Apollo's own GraphQL name for the same thing, established by capture, and is the strongest citation here. patternedOn means the SHAPE is Apollo's, recovered from the record, while the noun is documented separately: every recovered XPage names its collection after the plural entity it pages, so ApolloPlanPage.plans follows Apollo's convention rather than one Conduit chose. documentedBy means Apollo's public documentation describes the concept. A field with none of the three would be Conduit's own idea carrying no Apollo claim at all; there are currently none, which is a finding rather than a design. Where Apollo names something Conduit had named itself, the invention is DISPLACED by Apollo's name -- evidence displaces invention whichever way it arrives. Every entry is still displaced automatically the moment a capture recovers the same coordinate.",
  "provenanceTier": "CONDUIT_NATIVE",
  "cardinality": "A native field may set \"list\": true. Conduit establishes its own collections, so it states their shape. Observed fields never do: validation probing cannot see through a list type, so the recovery record never established one.",
